    ".XLF",
    "XLIFF Document",
    "3.7",
    "XML formatted file based on the XLIFF (XML Localisation Interchange File Format) specification developed by the OASIS Technical Committee; used as a standard means of exchanging localizable data and related information in a lossless format. Each XLIFF document contains one or more <file> elements. These elements identify the location of data sources, such as images, databases, properties files, etc. Windows OmegaT. Maxprograms Swordfish. Any text editor Mac OmegaT. Maxprograms Swordfish. Any text editor Linux OmegaT. Maxprograms Swordfish. Any text editor.",
