    ".CAV",
    "Comodo Virus Definitions File",
    "3.6",
    "File used by Comodo Internet Security, a free antivirus program used to protect computers against malware; contains signatures that are used to recognize viruses; used to update virus definitions when new viruses are discovered. CAV files commonly have the name bases.cav and are located in the following installation directory: COMODO/​COMODO Internet Security/​scanners. Windows Comodo Group Internet Security.",
