    "Data file created with SenTest, a scientific application used for sensitivity testing and data analysis; contains the results of tests conducted with sensitivity recording equipment. Sensitivity tests are used in automotive, aerospace, mining, and other fields. They are also used to test the the effectiveness and maximum permissible safe level of drugs, medicines, and pesticides. In biological fields, sensitivity tests are also called LD50 or LC50 tests. Windows Neyer Software SenTest. Data archive that contains an internal header followed by compressed binary data; created with Scifer, a data compression and archiving application; uses a new data compression logic based on Universal Common Logic (UCL). NOTE: SEN archives store the header within the file, while.BA files store the header information in a separate file. Windows Scifer.",
