    "3.2",
    "File used by FirstBreak, a program that tests the strengths of concrete mixes; contains the test results of concrete batches, including the batch reference, date, test specimen strengths, slump, air content, and temperature. TDT files are used for logging concrete tests and providing input into FirstBreak statistical analysis tests. They are stored in a.CSV format. Windows LogicSphere FirstBreak. Thumbnail file created by Sony and Panasonic digital camcorders; contains thumbnail stills of recorded video in the AVCHD (Advanced Video Coding High Definition) format; appears in folder when connecting camcorder to computer; not meant to be manually opened. TDT files can be found, along with.TID files, in the AVCHDTN folder, which is held within the AVCHD folder, which is held in the Private folder contained within your camcorder. THUMB.TDT - Only name of Sony/Panasonic TDT files. Mac Appears in folders in window when connecting Sony/Panasonic camcorder or memory card to computer. Windows Appears in folders in window when connecting Sony/Panasonic camcorder or memory card to computer. File created by Sim Tower: The Vertical Empire, a tower construction and management simulator; contains tower gameplay data such as a bank, office, cinema, or hotel; not meant to be manually opened. NOTE: Sim Tower was developed for Windows and Macintosh and released in 1994. It is no longer maintained. If you want open the application you will need a DOS emulator such as DOSBox. Mac Maxis Sim Tower: The Vertical Empire. Windows Maxis Sim Tower: The Vertical Empire. Linux Maxis Sim Tower: The Vertical EmpireFree. THOR Data Tree (TDT) file used by THOR-Merlin, a database program used to store and retrieve chemical information; contains data similar to a thesaurus that relates chemical information and concepts. TDT files are used to relate information and transmit information between programs that use different languages and terms. They are stored in a plain text format, but are not easily human-readable due to their custom syntax. Windows Daylight THOR-Merlin System.",
