    ".SDP",
    "Session Description Protocol File",
    "3.0",
    "Informational file created with media broadcasting software; contains the format, timing, and authorship of the streamed media; may be created for live streaming media with a program like Sorenson Broadcaster or for prerecorded media using a program like PlaylistBroadcaster. NOTE: In order for SDP information to be transmitted with the streaming media, the SDP file must be stored in the designated media directory on the streaming server. Windows RealNetworks RealPlayer 20/20. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Macgo Mac Media Player. VideoLAN VLC media playerFree. Presentation file originally created by StarOffice, the predecessor to the Apache OpenOffice office suite; saves a series of slides, often including a master or title slide and content slides. SDP files have been replaced by the.ODP format in Apache OpenOffice and other open source variants of the office suite. However, Apache OpenOffice can still load SDP files. NOTE: Apache OpenOffice was previously known as OpenOffice.org. Windows OpenOffice Impress. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Impress. Planamesa NeoOffice. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Impress. LibreOfficeFree.",
