    ".NPT",
    "Portfolio NetPublish Template",
    "3.0",
    "Precursor template for creating a Portfolio NetPublish project; includes a pre-designed Web interface and executable scripts that can be published to the Web; contains customizable sections, usually denoted by [[..]], for inserting custom code and image references. The customized version of the project is saved as an.NP file. Windows Extensis Portfolio NetPublish Mac Extensis Portfolio NetPublish. An NPT file is a schedule created by NetPoint, a program used to plan projects and schedules. It contains a schedule, which includes dates, colors, and timeline configuration. NPT files were replaced by.NP4 files, which were introduced in version 4 of NetPoint. NPT files are used by versions 1, 2, and 3 of NetPoint to store schedules. Even though NPT files were replaced by NP4 files in version 4, NetPoint can open NPT files. The program can also create NPT files but they are created to store backups of schedules. NetPoint is used for a variety of schedules and projects, such as a construction of a building, a development of a website, or events during a wedding day. You can analyze work tasks, schedule dates, organize activities, and layout yearlong plans. Windows PMA Technologies NetPoint.",
    "Windows Extensis Portfolio NetPublish. Mac Extensis Portfolio NetPublish. Windows PMA Technologies NetPoint.",
