    ["data_files",
    ".SPV",
    "SPSS Output Document",
    "2.9",
    "Data file generated by SPSS statistical analysis software; contains the output generated from data analytics functions run within SPSS; may store datasets, reports, charts, and other visualizations; can be viewed with SPSS versions 16 and later. NOTE: SPV files are generated by SPSS 16 and later and are not backwards compatible with earlier versions of SPSS. Previous versions of SPSS saved output files with an.SPO extension. Windows IBM SPSS. Mac IBM SPSS. Linux IBM SPSS. An SPV file is a SPIR-V module. It contains a shader used to give depth to 3D graphics. Graphics APIs like Vulkan, OpenCL, and OpenGL use SPV files to render 3D objects. Standard Portable Intermediate Representation V (SPIR-V) is a binary intermediate language for graphical shaders and compute kernels. Khronos Group released SPIR-V in 2015, replacing the original version of SPIR. Developers using SPIR-V save shader modules as SPV files. For example, developers can use Khronos Groups Glslang tool to convert.HLSL shaders into SPV files. These files contain a list of capabilities, global interfaces, entry points, and functions that determine how the shader affects an objects appearance. You can use Khronos Group SPIR-V Tools (multiplatform) to parse, disassemble, validate, and optimize SPV files. Windows Khronos Group SPIR-V Tools. Khronos Group SPIRV-Cross. Mac Khronos Group SPIR-V Tools. Khronos Group SPIRV-Cross. Linux Khronos Group SPIR-V Tools. Khronos Group SPIRV-CrossFree.",
    "Windows IBM SPSS. Mac IBM SPSS. Linux IBM SPSS. Windows Khronos Group SPIR-V Tools. Khronos Group SPIRV-Cross. Mac Khronos Group SPIR-V Tools. Khronos Group SPIRV-Cross. Linux Khronos Group SPIR-V Tools. Khronos Group SPIRV-Cross.",
    "Khronos Group SPIRV-Cross (multiplatform) can convert SPV shaders to the following formats:.GLSL - GLSL Shader.HLSL - High Level Shader Language MSL - Metal Shading Langague.JSON - JavaScript Object Notation."],
