    ".PCAPNG",
    "Pcap-NG Packet Capture File",
    "2.9",
    "Packet capture format that contains a dump of data packets captured over a network; saved in the PCAP Next Generation file format, a standard format for storing captured data. Each PCAPNG file contains several blocks or data, which contain different types of information. Examples of blocks include the section header block, interface description block, enhanced packet block, simple packet block, name resolution block, and interface statistics block. These blocks can be used to rebuild captured packets into recognizable data. NOTE: Pcap-NG is designed to previous Pcap (.PCAP) packet capture format. Wireshark began using the Pcap-NG file format in version 1.8. Windows Wireshark. Netresec CapLoader. Mac Wireshark. Linux WiresharkFree.",
